    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of The Army Act, 1950\n\nKey Provisions:\n1.\tApplication of the Act: \no\tApplies to officers, soldiers, and other persons subject to Army law. \no\tDefines the categories of personnel who come under the jurisdiction of the Act. \n2.\tConstitution and Control of the Army: \no\tProvides for the organization and maintenance of the Indian Army under the authority of the Central Government. \no\tRegulates the appointment, command, duties, and service obligations of Army personnel. \n3.\tDuties and Discipline: \no\tEstablishes rules relating to obedience of lawful commands, discipline, conduct, and military duties. \no\tEnsures that Army personnel maintain the required standards of efficiency and operational readiness. \n4.\tMilitary Offences: \no\tDefines various offences under Army law, including: \n\tDesertion and absence without leave. \n\tMutiny and disobedience of lawful commands. \n\tInsubordination and misconduct. \n\tActs prejudicial to good order and military discipline. \n5.\tPunishments and Penalties: \no\tProvides punishments for offences committed by persons subject to the Act. \no\tPunishments may include imprisonment, dismissal from service, reduction in rank, forfeiture of pay and allowances, and other disciplinary measures. \n6.\tCourt-Martial System: \no\tProvides for the constitution and functioning of military courts, including General Court-Martial, District Court-Martial, Summary General Court-Martial, and Summary Court-Martial. \no\tEstablishes procedures for investigation, trial, confirmation, and review of sentences. \n7.\tPowers of Commanding Officers: \no\tGrants powers to commanding officers to maintain discipline and deal with offences committed by personnel under their command. \no\tProvides for summary proceedings in specified cases. \n8.\tService Conditions and Administration: \no\tRegulates matters relating to enlistment, discharge, pay, allowances, leave, and other conditions of service. \no\tProvides mechanisms for effective administration of the Army. \n9.\tRule-Making Powers: \no\tEmpowers the Central Government to make rules and regulations regarding recruitment, service conditions, discipline, court procedures, and other matters connected with the Army.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
