    "dc.identifier.preamble_description" : [ {
      "value" : "<center style=\"font-size: 17px;\"> THE ARMY ACT, 1950</center> <center style=\"font-size: 16px;\">ACT NO. 46 OF 1950<sup>1</sup></center> <p style=\"text-align:right;\"> [20<i>th May, </i>1950.] </p> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span> An Act to consolidate and amend the law relating to the Government of the regular Army.<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span> <span style=\"margin-left: 15px;\"></span> BE it enacted by Parliament as follows:--<br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-top: 0;\"/>",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
    "dc.identifier.preamble_footnote" : [ {
      "value" : "<sup>1</sup>. This Act has been extended to-Goa, Daman and Diu with modifications by Reg. 12 of 1962, s. 3 and Schedule; Assam Rifles as modified by S.R.O. 318, dated 6-12-1962, <i>see</i> Gazette of India, Part II, s. 4, page 223. N.P. Pondicherry <i>vide</i> Reg. 7 of 1963, s. 3 and Schedule I (w.e.f. 1-10- 1963). And brought into force in Dadra and Nagar Haveli by Reg. 6 of 1963, s. 2 and Schedule I (w.e.f. 1-7-1965). <br/><hr style=\"border: none; margin-bottom: 3px; margin-top: 0;\"/>",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
